---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import {SITE} from '../data/tools.mjs';
const ld=[{'@type':'WebPage',name:'Privacy Policy',url:SITE+'/privacy-policy/'}];
---
<Page title="Privacy Policy | WorldsBestFreeTools" desc="How WorldsBestFreeTools handles your data: most tools run in your browser, we do not require accounts, and we explain every case where data is sent to a server or a third party." path="/privacy-policy/" ld={ld}>
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="meta">Last updated: 20 November 2026</p>
<p>This Privacy Policy explains what information WorldsBestFreeTools ("we", "us", "our") collects when you use <b>worldsbestfreetools.online</b> (the "Site"), how we use it, and the choices you have. The short version: you do not need an account, and most tools process your files and numbers inside your own browser without sending them to us.</p>

<div class="note"><b>In short:</b> we do not sell your personal data, we do not run advertising or tracking cookies today, and we do not store the files you process or the values you type into calculators. The few features that do send data to a server are listed in section 3.</div>

<h2>1. Information we do not collect</h2>
<ul>
<li>We do not ask you to register, so we hold no usernames, passwords or profiles.</li>
<li>Files you open in tools such as the image compressor, PDF tools, OCR, video tools and QR generator are processed locally in your browser and are not uploaded to us.</li>
<li>Numbers and text you type into calculators, converters and generators stay in your browser.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
<h3>a) Information you send us</h3>
<p>If you use the <a href="/contact-us/">Contact Us</a> form, we receive your <b>name</b>, <b>email address</b> and <b>message</b>. We use them only to read and reply to your message, to investigate problems you report and to keep a record of the conversation. Please do not put sensitive information in your message.</p>
<h3>b) Technical and usage data</h3>
<p>When you load a page, our hosting provider and servers automatically process technical data such as your IP address, browser and device type, the page requested, the referring page and the time of the request. This is needed to deliver the Site, keep it secure and prevent abuse. We also record simple, aggregated visit counts (for example, how many visits came from people and how many from search engines or AI crawlers, and which pages automated visitors request). These counters do not identify you and are not used to build a profile of you.</p>
<h3>c) Local storage and cookies</h3>
<p>We do not set advertising or analytics cookies. The Site stores small preferences on your own device:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Who sets it</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Language cookie (<code>googtrans</code>) and a saved language value</td><td>Remembers the language you chose in the translator so pages stay translated.</td><td>The Site, used by Google Translate</td></tr>
<tr><td>Saved currency value in local storage</td><td>Remembers the currency symbol you picked in finance calculators.</td><td>The Site</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>You can delete these at any time in your browser settings. Doing so simply resets the language and currency to the defaults.</p>

<h2>3. Features that send data to a server or third party</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>What is sent</th><th>To whom</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Contact form</td><td>Name, email, message</td><td>Our server and an email delivery service, so the message reaches us</td></tr>
<tr><td>Paraphrasing tool</td><td>The text you enter (up to 2,000 characters)</td><td>Our server, which forwards it to an AI provider (Anthropic) to produce the rewritten text. We do not intentionally store the text. Do not enter confidential information.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Language translator</td><td>The visible text of the page you are viewing, once you choose a language</td><td>Google Translate (Google LLC), which is loaded only after you pick a language. Google's own privacy policy applies to that translation.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Currency Converter and USD to INR</td><td>A request for current exchange rates (no personal data from you, but your IP address is visible to the rate provider as for any web request)</td><td>open.er-api.com</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tools that load models, libraries or fonts (for example OCR, background removal, video tools, PDF signing)</td><td>A download request for the required files; your own files are not sent</td><td>Public content delivery networks such as jsDelivr and Google Fonts</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hosting and security</td><td>Standard server logs</td><td>Our hosting provider (Vercel)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Visit counters</td><td>Aggregated counts only</td><td>A database service provider used to store the counts</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>When your browser contacts a third party, that party can see your IP address and basic browser details and may set its own cookies. We do not control those practices; please read their privacy policies.</p>

<h2>4. How we use information</h2>
<ul>
<li>To provide, maintain and improve the Site and its tools.</li>
<li>To respond to messages, bug reports and tool suggestions.</li>
<li>To keep the Site secure, limit abuse such as spam and excessive automated requests, and troubleshoot errors.</li>
<li>To understand overall usage so we can decide which tools to improve or add.</li>
<li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>Where the law requires a legal basis (for example under the GDPR), we rely on our legitimate interest in running and securing the Site, on your consent when you contact us or choose to use a third-party-backed feature, and on legal obligation where applicable.</p>

<h2>5. Sharing</h2>
<p>We do not sell, rent or trade your personal information. We share data only with service providers that help us run the Site (hosting, email delivery, the AI service used by the paraphrasing tool, and the storage service for visit counters), when you use a feature that involves a third party as described above, or when required by law or to protect our rights, users or the public.</p>

<h2>6. Retention</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Contact messages:</b> kept for as long as needed to answer you and handle follow-up, then deleted. You can ask us to delete your message sooner.</li>
<li><b>Server logs:</b> kept by our hosting provider for a limited period under its own retention rules.</li>
<li><b>Aggregated counters:</b> contain no personal data and may be kept indefinitely.</li>
<li><b>Preferences on your device:</b> stay until you clear them.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Security</h2>
<p>The Site is served over HTTPS. Because most tools run locally in your browser, your files and calculator inputs never leave your device. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

<h2>8. Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live (for example India under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, the European Economic Area and UK under the GDPR, or certain US states), you may have the right to access the personal data we hold about you, correct it, delete it, object to or restrict certain processing, withdraw consent, and complain to a data protection authority. To exercise any of these rights, contact us through the <a href="/contact-us/">Contact Us</a> page. We may need to verify your identity before acting on a request.</p>

<h2>9. Children</h2>
<p>The Site is a general-audience utility and is not directed at children under 13 (or the higher minimum age in your country). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has sent us personal information, please contact us and we will delete it.</p>

<h2>10. International transfers</h2>
<p>Our service providers may process data in countries other than your own, including countries whose data protection laws differ from yours. Where required, we use providers that apply appropriate safeguards.</p>

<h2>11. Links to other websites</h2>
<p>Pages may link to other websites. We are not responsible for their content or privacy practices.</p>

<h2>12. Advertising</h2>
<p>We do not currently show advertising. If we introduce advertising or analytics that use cookies, we will update this policy, show any consent choices the law requires, and make the change clear before it takes effect.</p>

<h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date above shows when it last changed. Significant changes will be highlighted on the Site. Continuing to use the Site after an update means you accept the revised policy.</p>

<h2>14. Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy or your data? Use our <a href="/contact-us/">Contact Us</a> page.</p>
</Page>
